  "id": "portland",
  "intro": "Portland is where a big river, a mountain and a wind tunnel meet, and all three are on the air. The Columbia carries ocean-going ships eighty miles inland, so you get a working marine band a long way from the sea. Mount Hood sits an hour east with the region’s rescue traffic on the federal band. And the Gorge funnels wind hard enough that soaring, gliding and general aviation traffic are constant on a good day. The city itself has an unusually dense FM dial for its size.",
  "introz": "波特兰是大河、雪山和风口三者交汇的地方，三者都在频谱上。哥伦比亚河让远洋船只能上溯一百三十公里，所以离海很远却仍有一条真正繁忙的海事频段。胡德山在东面一小时车程外，山区救援通信在联邦频段上。哥伦比亚峡谷把风收束得极强，天气好时滑翔与通用航空的通话不断。城市本身的调频频段密度也远超同等规模的城市。",
